# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/between_stories.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@thread bram_corvin_feud
# en: The Ledger War
name [940dc3] = 记录簿之战
# en: Bram had written Corvin up eleven times in one term. Corvin had started writing back.
premise [2abeb9] = 布拉姆一个学期给科尔文记了十一次处分。科尔文开始还击了。
# en: Bram and Corvin went to war over the demerit ledger, and you stepped into the middle of it.
journal.1 [999971] = 布拉姆和科尔文为了处分记录簿开战，而你踏进了战场正中。
# en: Bram's ledger vanished. You found it in Corvin's coat and put it back before anyone knew.
journal.2 [1dd23d] = 布拉姆的记录簿不见了。你在科尔文的外套里找到了它，赶在任何人发现之前放了回去。
# en: Bram's ledger vanished, and you let it stay vanished. The castle held its breath for a week.
journal.3 [b99d15] = 布拉姆的记录簿不见了，你让它继续不见。整个城堡屏息了一个星期。
# en: The headmistress set them to clear the confiscation vault together. You locked the door on them for an hour.
journal.4 [88ade8] = 院长让他们俩一起清理没收库。你把门锁上了一个小时。
# en: The headmistress set them to clear the confiscation vault together, and you watched them by the rules.
journal.5 [fa19ec] = 院长让他们俩一起清理没收库，你照规矩看着他们。
# en: Bram and Corvin shook hands in the vault doorway. Neither will say who offered first.
journal.6 [06cabb] = 布拉姆和科尔文在库房门口握了手。谁先伸的手，两人都不肯说。
# en: Bram and Corvin came out of the vault still enemies, if quieter ones.
journal.7 [45d414] = 布拉姆和科尔文走出库房时还是对头，只是安静了些。

@event feud_ledger_war
# en: Say Please
title [4ee6be] = 说“请”
# en: Bram has written Corvin up for the eleventh time this term ("existing in a corridor"), and Corvin has answered by charming the lock on Bram's demerit ledger so that it opens only for the word "please". Bram has been saying "OPEN" at it for ten minutes. Half the courtyard is watching. Both of them see you at the same moment.
text [e36d96] = 布拉姆这学期已经第十一次给科尔文记处分了（罪名是“在走廊里存在”），而科尔文的回应是给布拉姆的处分记录簿的锁施了个咒，只有听到“请”字才肯打开。布拉姆已经冲着它喊了十分钟“开！”。半个庭院的人都在看。两人同时看见了你。
# en: A courtyard fountain, a prefect shouting at a locked ledger in his hands, a grinning student leaning on the fountain rim with a deck of cards.
scene [44a364] = 庭院的喷泉边，一个级长冲着手里上了锁的记录簿大喊，一个咧嘴笑的学生拿着一副牌靠在喷泉边上。
# en: Step in between them
opt.left.label [d21ee8] = 站到他们中间
# en: "Just say it, Bram." Bram says it, through his teeth. The ledger opens. Corvin laughs so hard he has to hold on to the fountain, and Bram writes your name on a fresh page, very neatly, and underlines it.
opt.left.say.1 [51bfaa] = “说一声就行了，布拉姆。”布拉姆咬着牙说了。记录簿开了。科尔文笑得只好扶着喷泉，而布拉姆在新的一页上工工整整地写下你的名字，还划了条线。
# en: Keep walking
opt.right.label [6ca967] = 继续走
# en: You keep walking. Behind you, the courtyard counts along with Bram: "OPEN. OPEN." It's still going when you reach the library.
opt.right.say.1 [9adcc7] = 你继续往前走。身后，整个庭院跟着布拉姆一起数：“开！开！”你走到图书馆时，那边还没停。

@event feud_ledger_gone
# en: The Missing Ledger
title [42ed15] = 失踪的记录簿
# en: Bram's ledger has gone. Not locked: gone. Bram is white with fury and quoting rules at the walls. Corvin is very helpful about looking for it. Then you borrow Corvin's coat on a cold evening, and find the ledger in its inside pocket. Corvin is one detention from being sent home. If Bram finds it there, that's the end of him.
text [966b80] = 布拉姆的记录簿不见了。不是锁上了：是不见了。布拉姆气得脸色发白，对着墙壁背校规。科尔文帮着找，热心极了。后来一个冷天的晚上，你借了科尔文的外套，在内袋里摸到了那本记录簿。科尔文再挨一次禁闭就要被送回家。要是布拉姆在那儿找到它，科尔文就完了。
# en: A coat hanging on a dormitory peg with the corner of a red leather ledger sticking out of its pocket.
scene [771a96] = 宿舍挂钩上挂着一件外套，口袋里露出一本红色皮面记录簿的一角。
# en: Put it back quietly
opt.left.label [eb4271] = 悄悄放回去
# en: You leave it on Bram's desk in the prefects' room, open at today's page. Bram never knows how. Corvin knows exactly how. "Saint," he says, and for once it isn't quite a joke.
opt.left.say.1 [8a5865] = 你把它放在级长室布拉姆的桌上，翻到今天那一页。布拉姆始终不知道是怎么回事。科尔文完全知道是怎么回事。“圣人，”他说，这一次不全是玩笑。
# en: Leave it where it is
opt.right.label [e26ef5] = 就让它留在那儿
# en: You hang the coat back up. For a week nobody in the castle gets a demerit, and Bram stalks the corridors like a man who has lost a hand. Corvin buys everyone cider.
opt.right.say.1 [f35048] = 你把外套挂了回去。整整一个星期，城堡里没有一个人挨处分，布拉姆在走廊里游荡，像丢了一只手。科尔文请大家喝苹果酒。

@event feud_vault
# en: A Week in the Vault
title [52f8f0] = 没收库里的一周
# en: The headmistress has had enough of both of them. Bram and Corvin will clear out the confiscation vault together, every evening for a week, and you, having been seen in the middle of all of it, are to watch them. Twenty minutes in, Bram is labelling things. Corvin is unlabelling them.
text [b8ac7c] = 院长受够了他们俩。布拉姆和科尔文要一起清理没收库，连续一个星期，每个晚上；而你，因为被人看见一直夹在中间，负责看着他们。二十分钟后，布拉姆在给东西贴标签。科尔文在把标签撕掉。
# en: A cluttered vault of confiscated oddities, two students glaring at each other over a crate, a third leaning in the doorway with a lantern.
scene [c93751] = 堆满没收来的古怪物件的库房里，两个学生隔着一只板条箱怒目相对，第三个人提着灯靠在门口。
# en: Lock them in for an hour
opt.left.label [4e8357] = 把他们锁在里面一小时
# en: You step out "for a lantern" and turn the key. When you open the door an hour later they're sitting on the same crate, arguing about a confiscated board game, and Bram is winning, and Corvin is letting him.
opt.left.say.1 [89db9a] = 你说出去“拿盏灯”，转动了钥匙。一小时后你开门时，他们坐在同一只板条箱上，为一盘被没收的棋争论，布拉姆在赢，而科尔文在让他赢。
# en: Corvin hears the key turn and has the lock open before you've let go of it. "Nice try, saint." Bram writes you up for "obstruction of a punishment", which isn't a rule, until he invents it.
opt.left.say.2 [3dc95b] = 钥匙一转，科尔文就听见了，你还没松手他就把锁打开了。“不错的尝试，圣人。”布拉姆给你记了一笔“妨碍惩罚”，校规里本没有这一条，直到他发明了它。
# en: Watch them by the rules
opt.right.label [5ed0fb] = 照规矩看着他们
# en: You sit in the doorway and revise while they snipe. By the end of the week the vault is spotless and they've stopped speaking altogether, which is, the headmistress says, an improvement.
opt.right.say.1 [7c7c1f] = 你坐在门口复习，他们互相冷嘲热讽。到周末，库房一尘不染，两人干脆一句话都不说了——院长说，这是一种进步。

@event feud_end
# en: The Vault Door
title [b709f0] = 库房门口
# en: The last evening in the vault. {npc_rel(bram, corvin) > -20: Something has changed this week. Bram has stopped quoting rules at Corvin. Corvin has stopped quoting Bram back.|Nothing much has changed. They've cleared the vault by working at opposite ends of it.} At the door, Bram stops, and looks at Corvin, and then at you.
text [1a511e] = 在没收库的最后一个晚上。{npc_rel(bram, corvin) > -20: 这个星期有些东西变了。布拉姆不再对科尔文背校规。科尔文也不再学着背回去。|没什么变化。他们一人一头，把库房清完了。}到门口时，布拉姆停下来，看看科尔文，又看看你。
# en: Two students in a vault doorway at the end of a long week, one in a prefect's sash, one with cards behind his ear, a third watching.
scene [9eb3e9] = 漫长的一周结束时，两个学生站在库房门口，一个披着级长绶带，一个耳后夹着牌，第三个人在旁边看着。
# en: Say something to both of them
opt.left.label [4e97fd] = 对他们俩说点什么
# en: You say they make a better team than either would admit. Bram goes red. Corvin grins. Then Bram, stiffly, holds out a hand, and Corvin shakes it, and immediately palms the prefect's pencil. Bram lets him keep it.
opt.left.say.1 [39df83] = 你说，他们俩搭档起来比任何一个人愿意承认的都要好。布拉姆脸红了。科尔文咧嘴一笑。然后布拉姆僵硬地伸出手，科尔文握了握，顺手摸走了级长的铅笔。布拉姆让他留着了。
# en: You try. Bram says "noted". Corvin says "saint". They leave by different stairs. But the ledger, after that, has Corvin's name in it a little less often.
opt.left.say.2 [51d0c0] = 你试了。布拉姆说“已记录”。科尔文说“圣人”。两人从不同的楼梯离开。不过从那以后，科尔文的名字在记录簿上出现得少了一点。
# en: Leave them to it
opt.right.label [4dcfa4] = 让他们自己待着
# en: You go ahead up the stairs. Behind you, a long silence, and then Corvin's laugh, and then, astonishingly, Bram's. At breakfast they nod to each other. Nobody knows what to make of it.
opt.right.say.1 [71f0b3] = 你先上了楼。身后是长长的沉默，接着是科尔文的笑声，然后，令人惊讶地，是布拉姆的。早饭时，两人互相点了点头。谁都不知道该怎么看这件事。
# en: You leave them to it. Neither of them says goodbye to the other. The war is over, more or less, because both of them are tired of it.
opt.right.say.2 [0bb882] = 你让他们自己待着。两人谁也没跟对方道别。战争结束了，差不多吧，因为两人都打累了。

@thread tobias_mir
# en: The Watering Engine
name [da92b1] = 浇水机
# en: Mir built Tobias a machine to water the greenhouse. Then neither of them could stop talking about it.
premise [687e0b] = 米尔给托比亚斯造了一台给温室浇水的机器。然后两人都停不下来地聊它。
# en: Mir built Tobias a watering engine, and you noticed how long they spent explaining it to each other.
journal.1 [fa1e2f] = 米尔给托比亚斯造了一台浇水机，你注意到他们互相讲解它讲了多久。
# en: Tobias asked how to invite Mir to the orchard "without it being a thing". You helped him plan the thing.
journal.2 [ac6d7c] = 托比亚斯问你怎么请米尔去果园，“又不算那回事”。你帮他把“那回事”计划好了。
# en: Tobias asked how to invite Mir somewhere. You told him to just ask.
journal.3 [c23ec0] = 托比亚斯问你怎么请米尔出去。你让他直接去问。
# en: Mir wondered if Tobias only liked the engine. You told Mir otherwise.
journal.4 [75e416] = 米尔怀疑托比亚斯只是喜欢那台机器。你告诉米尔不是这样。
# en: Mir wondered if Tobias only liked the engine. You told Mir to ask him.
journal.5 [d413ba] = 米尔怀疑托比亚斯只是喜欢那台机器。你让米尔自己去问他。
# en: Tobias and Mir turned up at the orchard together. Whatever it is, it's their business, and it's going well.
journal.6 [57fed4] = 托比亚斯和米尔一起来到了果园。不管那是什么，那是他们的事，而且进展得很好。
# en: Tobias and Mir are the best of friends, and the greenhouse is the best-watered in the country.
journal.7 [d0f658] = 托比亚斯和米尔成了最好的朋友，那座温室是全国浇水最勤的温室。

@event tm_watering_engine
# en: The Watering Engine
title [da92b1] = 浇水机
# en: There's a brass contraption trundling along the greenhouse benches, watering seedlings with a little copper spout. Mir built it. Tobias is explaining to it, gently, which plants like it lower. Mir is listening to Tobias the way Mir usually listens only to machines. Neither of them has noticed you.
text [6c60c0] = 温室的工作台上，一台黄铜机器正慢吞吞地走着，用一个小铜嘴给幼苗浇水。是米尔造的。托比亚斯正温和地向它解释，哪些植物喜欢浇得低一点。米尔听托比亚斯说话的样子，平时只有听机器时才会那样。两人都没注意到你。
# en: A greenhouse with a brass contraption trundling along the benches watering seedlings, a big student and a goggled artificer crouched beside it, deep in talk.
scene [cf2ce3] = 温室里，一台黄铜机器沿着工作台给幼苗浇水，一个大个子学生和一个戴护目镜的工匠蹲在旁边聊得正起劲。
# en: Ask them how it works
opt.left.label [443201] = 问问它是怎么工作的
# en: They tell you at the same time, in different directions: Mir about gears, Tobias about ferns. They keep interrupting each other to agree. You leave an hour later. They don't notice that either.
opt.left.say.1 [f5e35d] = 他们同时开口，各讲各的：米尔讲齿轮，托比亚斯讲蕨类。两人不停地打断对方，为的是表示同意。一小时后你离开了。他们也没注意到。
# en: Leave them to it
opt.right.label [4dcfa4] = 让他们自己忙
# en: You take your notes to the far end of the greenhouse. The engine squeaks past you twice, followed by two people arguing happily about tomatoes.
opt.right.say.1 [288ace] = 你把笔记拿到温室另一头。那台机器吱吱呀呀地从你身边经过了两次，后面跟着两个为西红柿开心争论的人。

@event tm_invitation
# en: Not a Thing
title [007dd5] = 不算那回事
# en: Tobias corners you by the potting benches, turning his cap round and round in his big hands. "I'd like to ask Mir to the orchard on Sunday," he says. "To see the bees. Only, without it being a thing. Unless it's a thing. How do you do that?"
text [0e41c2] = 托比亚斯在育苗台边堵住你，一双大手把帽子转了又转。“我想请米尔星期天去果园，”他说，“去看蜜蜂。只是，又不算那回事。除非它就是那回事。这该怎么弄？”
# en: A big student sitting on an upturned flowerpot, turning his cap round and round in his hands, asking a friend for advice.
scene [b06e94] = 一个大个子学生坐在倒扣的花盆上，手里不停地转着帽子，向朋友讨主意。
# en: Help him plan it
opt.left.label [e52788] = 帮他计划
# en: You spend an evening on it: a picnic, a jar of honey, a spare pair of goggles in case of bees. Tobias writes it all down on a seed packet. He apologises for the trouble four times and thanks you seven.
opt.left.say.1 [e5be9f] = 你花了一个晚上：野餐，一罐蜂蜜，再备一副护目镜以防蜜蜂。托比亚斯把这些全写在一个种子袋上。他为给你添麻烦道歉了四次，道谢了七次。
# en: Tell him to just ask
opt.right.label [e662fc] = 让他直接去问
# en: "Just ask," you say. Tobias takes a breath that lifts his whole frame, and goes and asks. You hear Mir say "probably!" from across the greenhouse, which from Mir is a yes.
opt.right.say.1 [28f38c] = “直接问，”你说。托比亚斯深吸一口气，整个身板都挺了起来，然后去问了。你听见米尔在温室另一头说“大概吧！”——从米尔嘴里说出来，这就是答应。
# en: Tobias goes to ask, and comes back having talked about the engine for twenty minutes instead. "I'll ask tomorrow," he says. He does, in the end. It takes a week.
opt.right.say.2 [328841] = 托比亚斯去问了，回来时却是聊了二十分钟机器。“我明天再问，”他说。他最后还是问了。花了一个星期。

@event tm_misread
# en: Only the Engine?
title [d43b83] = 只是因为机器？
# en: Mir finds you, goggles pushed up, unusually quiet. "Tobias wants to go to the orchard. To see the bees." A long pause. "Is that about the engine? Probably it's about the engine. It's a very good engine. It's fine if it's about the engine."
text [345a4a] = 米尔来找你，护目镜推到额头上，难得这么安静。“托比亚斯想去果园。看蜜蜂。”长长的停顿。“这是因为那台机器吗？大概是因为机器吧。那是台很好的机器。要是因为机器，也没关系。”
# en: A workshop at night, an artificer sitting on a bench with goggles pushed up, staring at a half-built engine, a friend in the doorway.
scene [a19d46] = 夜里的工坊，一个工匠把护目镜推到额头上坐在长凳上，盯着一台半成品机器，朋友站在门口。
# en: Tell Mir it isn't
opt.left.label [2ae7a2] = 告诉米尔不是这样
# en: "It isn't about the engine," you say. Mir looks at you for a long moment, and then goes slowly pink from the collar up. "Oh," says Mir. "Oh. Probably I should bring something. Not the engine." You suggest honey.
opt.left.say.1 [3352e1] = “不是因为机器，”你说。米尔看了你很久，然后从领口开始慢慢红了上来。“哦，”米尔说，“哦。我大概该带点什么去。别带机器。”你建议带蜂蜜。
# en: "Ask him yourself."
opt.right.label [b2317d] = “你自己去问他。”
# en: Mir marches into the greenhouse and asks him, straight out, in front of a bench of seedlings. You don't hear the answer. You see Mir's face, after. That's enough.
opt.right.say.1 [9f828e] = 米尔大步走进温室，当着一工作台幼苗的面，直截了当地问了他。你没听见回答。你看见了米尔之后的表情。这就够了。
# en: Mir doesn't ask. Mir builds Tobias a second engine instead, a smaller one, for the windowsill. It's a kind of asking. You're not sure Tobias reads it.
opt.right.say.2 [284ce2] = 米尔没去问。米尔转而又给托比亚斯造了第二台机器，小一些的，放在窗台上用。这也算一种问法。你不确定托比亚斯看懂了没有。

@event tm_end
# en: The Orchard
title [f7870f] = 果园
# en: Sunday, the orchard, the bees. {npc_rel(tobias, mir) >= 30: Tobias and Mir arrive together, carrying a picnic between them and arguing happily about bees.|Tobias and Mir arrive separately, and spend the afternoon talking about the engine.} They've saved you a corner of the blanket, though you weren't sure you were invited.
text [4cf02b] = 星期天，果园，蜜蜂。{npc_rel(tobias, mir) >= 30: 托比亚斯和米尔一起来了，两人抬着一篮野餐，开开心心地争论着蜜蜂。|托比亚斯和米尔分头来了，整个下午都在聊那台机器。}他们在毯子上给你留了个角，虽然你也不确定自己是不是被邀请了。
# en: An orchard on a sunny afternoon, two friends on a blanket among beehives, one in goggles, one with a jar of honey, laughing.
scene [28f7e1] = 阳光明媚的午后果园，蜂箱之间铺着一条毯子，两个朋友坐在上面，一个戴着护目镜，一个拿着一罐蜂蜜，笑着。
# en: Stay for the picnic
opt.left.label [07dc2a] = 留下来野餐
# en: You stay an hour, and then slip away, and neither of them notices you go. Whatever it is, it's their business. It looks like it's going well.
opt.left.say.1 [99fc2e] = 你待了一个小时，然后悄悄溜走了，两人谁都没注意到你走了。不管那是什么，那是他们的事。看样子进展得很好。
# en: It's a lovely afternoon. Whatever it might have been, it's a friendship, and a good one: the greenhouse gets watered on time for the rest of the year.
opt.left.say.2 [e818a7] = 那是个美好的下午。不管它本可能是什么，它是一段友谊，而且是很好的一段：这一年剩下的日子里，温室都准时浇了水。
# en: Leave them the blanket
opt.right.label [cad02a] = 把毯子留给他们
# en: You say you've an essay, which is true. From the orchard gate you look back once. They're sharing the honey. You don't look back again.
opt.right.say.1 [2035e1] = 你说你有篇论文要写，这是真的。走到果园门口时，你回头看了一眼。他们在分着吃蜂蜜。你没有再回头。
# en: You leave them to the bees. At supper, they're still talking about the engine. Best friends, then. It's not nothing.
opt.right.say.2 [3aebeb] = 你把他们留给了蜜蜂。晚饭时，他们还在聊那台机器。那就是最好的朋友了。这也不算什么都没有。

@thread study_circle
# en: The Thursday Circle
name [6d1812] = 星期四学习会
# en: A study circle that started with two chairs and a borrowed lamp.
premise [8ca799] = 一个以两把椅子和一盏借来的灯开始的学习会。
# en: You and a friend started meeting in the library on Thursdays, with one lamp between you.
journal.1 [4aac88] = 你和一个朋友开始每个星期四在图书馆碰头，两人共用一盏灯。
# en: Someone nobody much liked asked to join. You said yes, and the circle got bigger.
journal.2 [44b2fa] = 一个大家都不太喜欢的人想加入。你说好，学习会变大了。
# en: Someone nobody much liked asked to join. The circle said no, and stayed cosy.
journal.3 [976ff1] = 一个大家都不太喜欢的人想加入。学习会拒绝了，依旧温馨。
# en: The night before exams, the circle nearly came apart. You held it together.
journal.4 [6c7f40] = 考试前一晚，学习会差点散了。你把它撑了下来。
# en: The night before exams, the circle came apart, and put itself back together after.
journal.5 [425704] = 考试前一晚，学习会散了，考完后又自己凑了回来。
# en: The Thursday Circle has its own table now, and a name carved under it.
journal.6 [7580b9] = 星期四学习会如今有了自己的桌子，桌子底下还刻着一个名字。

@event circle_founded
# en: Thursdays
title [6e5f2c] = 星期四
# en: {o} drops into the chair across from you in the library with a stack of books and a borrowed lamp. "I can't revise alone. I just read the same page. What if we did this every week? Thursdays. You and me, and whoever else."
text [ac19dc] = {o}抱着一摞书和一盏借来的灯，在图书馆里你对面的椅子上坐下。“我一个人复习不进去。同一页看了又看。要不我们每个星期都这样？星期四。你和我，再加上谁都行。”
# en: A library alcove in the evening, two students sharing a single lamp over open books, an empty third chair pulled up.
scene [d679a7] = 傍晚图书馆的壁龛里，两个学生在一盏灯下翻着书，旁边拉过来一把空着的第三把椅子。
# en: "Thursdays, then."
opt.left.label [dd5103] = “那就星期四。”
# en: You shake on it over the lamp. The first Thursday you get through a chapter each and an argument about it. The second Thursday someone else asks if the third chair is taken.
opt.left.say.1 [19a427] = 你们隔着灯握手为定。第一个星期四，你们各读完一章，还为此吵了一架。第二个星期四，有人来问第三把椅子有没有人。
# en: "I work better alone."
opt.right.label [b2a822] = “我一个人效率更高。”
# en: {o} nods, and takes the lamp to another alcove. You get a great deal done. Every Thursday after that you see the lamp lit in the far alcove, and sometimes two heads under it.
opt.right.say.1 [234137] = {o}点点头，把灯拿到另一个壁龛去了。你完成了很多。之后的每个星期四，你都能看见远处那个壁龛亮着灯，有时灯下是两个脑袋。

@event circle_newcomer
# en: The Fourth Chair
title [bd4b61] = 第四把椅子
# en: The circle is four now, sometimes five. Tonight {n} is hovering at the end of the table with an armful of books: {n}, whom nobody in the circle much likes, and who has, it turns out, failed the last two practicals. "Could I sit in?" {n} asks. The others look at you.
text [cb7a3d] = 学习会现在有四个人了，有时五个。今晚，{n}抱着一堆书在桌子尽头徘徊：学习会里没人太喜欢这个人，而且原来{n}最近两次实践课都没过。“我能坐下来一起吗？”{n}问。其他人都看着你。
# en: A library table with three students around a lamp, a fourth standing a little way off with books clutched to their chest.
scene [e380e9] = 图书馆的桌边，三个学生围着一盏灯，第四个人站在不远处，把书紧紧抱在胸前。
# en: "Pull up a chair."
opt.left.label [368005] = “拉把椅子过来。”
# en: {n} sits down. It's stiff for a week. Then {n} explains, better than any of you, the one thing all of you had wrong, and the circle shifts round to make room.
opt.left.say.1 [5147b2] = {n}坐了下来。头一个星期很僵。后来{n}把一件你们大家都弄错了的事讲得比谁都明白，于是学习会挪了挪，腾出了位置。
# en: "We're full, sorry."
opt.right.label [c199d1] = “抱歉，满了。”
# en: {n} says "of course" and goes. The circle stays as it was, cosy and quick. You see {n} revising alone the next Thursday, at the far end of the room.
opt.right.say.1 [6bfaa8] = {n}说了句“当然”，走了。学习会还是老样子，温馨又高效。下个星期四，你看见{n}一个人在房间另一头复习。

@event circle_exam_night
# en: The Night Before
title [6e1f49] = 前一晚
# en: The night before exams the circle sits till the lamps are trimmed, and it goes wrong. {w} hasn't done the notes {w.they} promised, and somebody says so, loudly, and {w} says some things back. Half the table is on its feet.
text [bf85b2] = 考试前一晚，学习会一直坐到灯芯都剪短了，然后出了问题。{w}没做完{w.they}答应要做的笔记，有人大声说了出来，{w}也回了几句难听的。半张桌子的人都站了起来。
# en: A library table late at night strewn with notes and cold tea, students glaring at each other across it, one of them on their feet.
scene [f23605] = 深夜的图书馆桌上散落着笔记和凉掉的茶，学生们隔着桌子怒目相视，其中一人站了起来。
# en: Hold it together
opt.left.label [6430cd] = 把大家拢住
# en: You split {w}'s chapter four ways and start reading it aloud before anyone can leave. By midnight it's done, and {w} brings everyone breakfast the next morning without being asked.
opt.left.say.1 [7982f1] = 你把{w}那一章分成四份，在任何人离开之前就开始大声朗读。到午夜就完成了，第二天早上{w}没人要求就给大家带来了早饭。
# en: You try, but it's too late and too tired. The circle breaks up at the door. You revise alone till two. It comes back together after the exams, a little shy of itself.
opt.left.say.2 [c2aca6] = 你试了，可太晚了，大家也太累了。学习会在门口散了。你一个人复习到两点。考完后它又凑了回来，彼此都有点不好意思。
# en: Take {w}'s chapter yourself
opt.right.label [2a8c0d] = 把{w}那一章揽下来
# en: "I'll do it," you say, and the table goes quiet. You're up till three. {w} sits up with you, not saying much, and makes the tea.
opt.right.say.1 [4c7ba6] = “我来做，”你说，桌边安静了下来。你熬到了三点。{w}陪你坐着，没说什么，一直在泡茶。

@event circle_last
# en: The Carved Table
title [870a51] = 刻字的桌子
# en: The Thursday Circle has outlasted the term. It has its own table now, and its own lamp, which the librarian pretends not to know about. Someone has brought a penknife and suggests, in a whisper, that the table should have a name on it. Underneath, where nobody will see.
text [06ff03] = 星期四学习会撑过了这个学期。它现在有了自己的桌子，还有自己的灯，图书管理员假装不知道。有人带了把小刀，压低声音提议，这张桌子该刻上个名字。刻在底下，没人看得见的地方。
# en: A library table in the evening, a group of students round a lamp, one of them carving something small into the underside of the table with a penknife.
scene [d47f52] = 傍晚图书馆的桌边，一群学生围着一盏灯，其中一人正用小刀在桌子底面刻着什么小字。
# en: Carve it
opt.left.label [9be41d] = 刻上去
# en: You carve "THURSDAYS" on the underside of the table, very small, while the others keep lookout. Years from now somebody will find it and wonder. You hope they start a circle.
opt.left.say.1 [5fd719] = 你在桌子底面刻下小小的“星期四”，其他人帮你望风。多年以后，会有人发现它，好奇它的来历。你希望那人也办一个学习会。
# en: Leave the table be
opt.right.label [230a14] = 别动这张桌子
# en: You talk them out of the penknife. Somebody writes "Thursdays" on the inside cover of a library book instead, in pencil, and puts it back on the shelf where it'll be found by the right person.
opt.right.say.1 [fb555a] = 你劝他们收起了小刀。有人改用铅笔在一本图书馆藏书的封面内页写下“星期四”，再把书放回架上，等着对的人去发现。
